0..75 Comment "// Rose trees: a node holds its children, in two forms. Written directly, a"
76..154 Comment "// node holds a `List` of nodes: the list\'s parameter is strictly positive, so"
155..232 Comment "// each child stands below the node and the family declares (#517); a measure"
233..303 Comment "// recurses through the list\'s `map`, which a call instantiates at the"
304..379 Comment "// children\'s stage (#393), and a run passes `map` the children\'s type as a"
380..450 Comment "// code (#452). Written as a block, a node holds a forest and a forest"
451..526 Comment "// is empty or a tree before a forest: the two families name each other, so"
527..600 Comment "// they are one block, admitted as one and sharing one stage; and the two"
601..676 Comment "// measures name each other, so they are one fixpoint over the sum of their"
677..750 Comment "// domains, each measure that fixpoint at its own summand. A call through"
751..826 Comment "// either stands one stage below the node or forest it was read from (Abel,"
827..906 Comment "// _Termination checking with types_, doi:10.1051/ita:2004015). What the direct"
907..966 Comment "// form refuses is in `../../pathological/data/rose.gandr`."
968..1040 Comment "// The naturals the measures count in, their addition, and the lists the"
1041..1070 Comment "// direct form nests through."
1071..1077 Keyword "import"
1078..1079 StringLit "\""
1079..1096 StringLit "./data-base.gandr"
1096..1097 StringLit "\""
1098..1099 Other ";"
